  "notes": [
    "Response latency percentiles cover dispatched requests with responses. Durable latency percentiles cover observed attempts and terminals, including drain; timings are sampled upper bounds. Dropped offers have no latency observation.",
    "All-drained describes admitted work, not completion of offers dropped by the client; inspect dispatched and dropped counts and liveness_pass.",
    "Late throughput excludes drain. Timing and proxy counters use their own post-warmup samples, differing by scrape duration.",
    "Histogram observations overlap and are not wall-time utilization. SQL acknowledgement includes a SQL commit already counted by sql_commit.",
    "Counter-window per-admission figures normalize work; they do not attribute each call to the newly admitted cohort.",
    "Absent phases were not instrumented or had no observations. In particular, missing baseline lane_wait is not evidence of zero candidate queueing.",
    "The mixed workload deliberately includes one reverting EVM call in three; aggregate eth_estimateGas errors alone do not prove transport failure.",
    "A lower serial_wait alone cannot show fairness improved: include lane_wait and health_capacity_wait, end-to-end latency, attempted progress, and backlog."
  ],
